From feac25a3541a9084475a052ea281556d004428f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 22:14:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09313/11362] Correct tonight's changelog: vLLM serves as of
 v33

The entry closed with "vLLM has not yet served on Kaggle; v32 is in flight". v32 failed and
v33 is the one that worked: server up in 415s, admission exact at 155472, and 24/24
requests round-tripping through the translation layer at a worst-case prompt.

Records the last two defects. libcuda was sought via ldconfig, which lists none in that
container, when the CUDA wheels ship a stub for exactly this purpose. And the one that
would have failed every run from v28 onward by itself: the vLLM launcher called the
llama.cpp health check, which tests for "ok" in the response body -- vLLM answers 200 with
an empty body, so v32 served 157 consecutive health 200s while the launcher waited out its
whole budget and reported failure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
